   478	3. **The runner discarded the model's responses.** It kept the score and the token
   479	   counts, so `correct=False` was an indistinguishable zero: you could not tell whether
   480	   the model lost track of state — what the experiment measures — or miscopied a JSON
   481	   field. With responses retained, adjudicating 45 failures across four traces of one
   482	   cell gives **32 wrong-shelf (71 %), 7 wrong action type (16 %), 5 field-copy errors
   483	   (11 %), 1 unparseable**.
   484	4. **A truncated episode counted as complete.** Aggregation counted files, not steps; an
   485	   episode of 163 steps out of 200 entered the mean. The bias was two thousandths, but
   486	   it was only found because completeness was checked as a matter of routine.
   487	5. **Traces that did not record their own conditions.** For most of this work the traces
   488	   stored no output cap, reasoning budget, provider or responding model ID. Two files
   489	   from the same cell could come from different caps and nothing would say so — which is
   490	   how a −5.8-point "environment effect" survived long enough to be written down. The
   491	   runners now write a conditions header and per-step token usage — but **only runs made
   492	   after that change carry it**: the 367 traces behind the tables in this draft do not,
   493	   so their conditions are certified by the filename and the run log, not by the
   494	   artefact itself.
   495	6. **A probe that measured the wrong pattern.** The cache probe repeated an identical
   496	   request and concluded that Vertex has no implicit cache, while the project's own
   497	   grids recorded 503,600 cached tokens in one episode. The probe was correct; the
   498	   pattern it probed was not the one the experiment uses.
   499	
   500	A third block, found while measuring the second model, contains the most expensive
   501	artefact of the project:
   502	
   503	7. **One of the four arms never ran.** Stateful read its state patch with a non-greedy
   504	   regex that stopped at the first closing brace. Every nested patch — the normal case,
   505	   `{"shelf_contents": {"3": {...}}}` — was truncated, failed to parse, and was dropped
   506	   without a warning: **40 of 5,773 applied on Gemini, 0 of 6,000 on Haiku**. What both
   507	   Stateful columns measured is full history plus a state block with no inventory — empty
   508	   on Haiku, and on Gemini holding only the occasional `last_event` (the 40 patches, in
   509	   11 episodes). Its unit test
   510	   used a flat value and passed. It surfaced only because Stateful beat SKILL.state on
   511	   Haiku and we went to the traces to find out why. Re-measured with the parser fixed,
   512	   no change was detected (§3). The first fix was itself incomplete: on Haiku it still
   513	   dropped every patch written in Markdown — 731 of 3,000 at T=200 — which the third
   514	   adversarial review found, not us; a third parser version closed it. A defect that
   515	   changes nothing measurable is still a defect in what the column claims to measure.
   516	8. **A cap one model respects and the other does not.** The summariser's own cap was
   517	   never reached on Gemini and was exceeded in half the summaries on Haiku (§3). A cap
   518	   is not a neutral constant across models; it has to be checked per model, in the
   519	   traces.
   520	9. **Resuming re-paid finished work.** The completeness check counted the conditions
   521	   header as a step, so no episode ever matched its horizon and every relaunch re-ran
   522	   episodes already measured. It was caught on the first relaunch of R2 because a cell
   523	   finished minutes earlier started again.
   524	10. **The traces did not record cache writes.** The client received them; the trace row
   525	    did not store them. In the first run of the prompt-order experiment the arm that
   526	    rewrites its cache every step — the most expensive case — showed ~540 prompt tokens
   527	    per step and looked the cheapest. Those twelve episodes were discarded and re-run.
   528	    The §4 table does not depend on it: it was computed by the grid runner, which counted
   529	    writes.
